        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಬುಟ್ಟಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬುಟ್ಟಿ (buṭṭi) — \"a basket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Woven, usually from bamboo, and carried on the hip or the head rather than in the hand. ಹಣ್ಣಿನ ಬುಟ್ಟಿ (buṭṭi) is a basket of fruit; a ಹೂವಿನ ಬುಟ್ಟಿ (buṭṭi) is what flowers come to the door in."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The little -ina in the middle of those is the joining piece Kannada slips between two names to say the second belongs to the first. Fruit-of basket. You can build the same shape with anything you already have."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬುಟ್ಟಿ (buṭṭi) shares its ending with the ಚಾಪೆ (cāpe)'s world rather than the ಕುರ್ಚಿ's: another light, cheap, repairable thing made from what grows nearby, and one that a house replaces every few years without thinking about it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: a thing to sit on, and a thing to carry with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
